+# CONTRACT — Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a new doc -> test: `get(id)` returns deep-equal content
+- [ ] `create` throws if id already exists on current branch -> test: second `create` throws
+- [ ] `create` allowed after `delete` (id no longer exists) -> test: delete then create succeeds
+- [ ] `get` returns current content -> test: returns deep-equal of latest update
+- [ ] `get` returns a deep clone (mutating result doesn't affect store) -> test: mutate returned obj, re-get unchanged
+- [ ] `get` throws if doc doesn't exist -> test: throws on unknown id
+- [ ] `get` throws if doc deleted -> test: delete then get throws
+- [ ] `update` replaces content + creates a version -> test: get reflects new content; history grows by 1
+- [ ] `update` throws if doc doesn't exist -> test: throws on unknown id
+- [ ] `update` throws if doc deleted -> test: delete then update throws
+- [ ] `delete` removes doc -> test: get after delete throws
+- [ ] `delete` throws if doc doesn't exist -> test: throws on unknown id
+- [ ] `delete` throws if already deleted -> test: double delete throws
+- [ ] Stored content is deep-cloned on write (mutating input doesn't affect store) -> test: mutate input after create, get unchanged
+
+## Version History
+- [ ] `create` generates a version with unique id, timestamp, content -> test: history length 1, fields present
+- [ ] `update` generates a new version -> test: history length grows; each id unique
+- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions oldest-first -> test: timestamps non-decreasing, order matches op order
+- [ ] version ids are unique -> test: all ids distinct
+- [ ] `getHistory` throws for unknown doc -> test: throws
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content at that version -> test: returns the historical content (clone)
+- [ ] `getVersion` returns deep clone -> test: mutate result, store unchanged
+- [ ] `getVersion` throws for unknown version -> test: throws
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] default branch is `"main"` -> test: `getBranch()` === "main" initially
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state -> test: docs visible on new branch
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from given branch -> test: uses fromBranch state regardless of current
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws on duplicate name -> test: throws
+- [ ] `switchBranch` changes active branch -> test: getBranch reflects it
+- [ ] `switchBranch` throws on unknown branch -> test: throws
+- [ ] CRUD applies to active branch only -> test: change on branch B not seen on main
+- [ ] branches are isolated (deep copy at fork) -> test: update on child doesn't change parent
+- [ ] `listBranches()` lists all branch names -> test: contains created branches
+
+## Merging (three-way)
+- [ ] no changes on either side -> no-op, applied true, no conflicts -> test
+- [ ] only source changed a field -> take theirs, applied true -> test
+- [ ] only ours changed a field -> keep ours, applied true -> test
+- [ ] both changed same field to same value -> no conflict -> test
+- [ ] both changed same field to different values -> conflict, applied false, current unchanged -> test
+- [ ] nested fields merged structurally; non-conflicting nested changes combine -> test
+- [ ] conflict path is dot-separated (e.g. "a.b.c") -> test
+- [ ] Conflict has documentId, path, base, ours, theirs -> test fields correct
+- [ ] different docs changed on different branches merge cleanly -> test, no conflicts
+- [ ] added field on one side only -> taken -> test
+- [ ] deleted field on one side (other unchanged) -> removed in merged -> test
+- [ ] doc created only on source -> appears in merged & applied to current -> test
+- [ ] doc deleted on source (unchanged on ours) -> removed on merge -> test
+- [ ] when no conflicts, merge auto-applied to current branch (state persists) -> test: after merge get reflects merged
+- [ ] when conflicts, `merged` still returned with ours-resolution; current branch unchanged -> test
+- [ ] `merge` throws if sourceBranch unknown -> test
+- [ ] arrays treated atomically (different arrays conflict) -> test
+- [ ] common ancestor (LCA) correctly found across branch/merge topology -> test
+
+## Build / Lint
+- [ ] `npm run build` clean -> test: tsc exits 0
+- [ ] `npm run lint` clean -> test: eslint exits 0
+- [ ] `npm test` all pass -> test: vitest green
